Bye.

58
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:50,580
Bye.

59
00:02:55,049 --> 00:02:59,109
I guess that's not so bad, Tachibana. Better than Aoi over here.

60
00:02:59,469 --> 00:03:04,229
I heard you've been branded as a failure among forwards, and now they've got you playing defense.

61
00:03:04,489 --> 00:03:09,689
Man, that's pathetic. I always knew you'd turn out to be the most useless. Way to go.

62
00:03:10,289 --> 00:03:11,389
Hey, that's enough.

63
00:03:14,109 --> 00:03:16,009
You don't know what you're talking about.

64
00:03:16,749 --> 00:03:20,669
I'm on the same team as Tachibana and Otomo, and they're amazing players.

65
00:03:21,829 --> 00:03:23,789
I've thought so ever since the tryouts.

66
00:03:24,389 --> 00:03:29,049
Anyone who can't see that doesn't know jack about being a strong soccer player.

67
00:03:30,269 --> 00:03:34,089
That's so nice of you to say about your fellow teammates, Gold Star.

68
00:03:34,309 --> 00:03:35,469
But we were talking about you.

69
00:03:35,869 --> 00:03:39,549
I suppose it's hard being a waste of space on a team you barely play for.

70
00:03:40,109 --> 00:03:43,909
I may not be playing in matches now, but I'm polishing my skills.

71
00:03:44,369 --> 00:03:46,229
He'll be a tough day for you when I return.

72
00:03:47,849 --> 00:03:49,629
As a fullback, sure.

73
00:03:50,229 --> 00:03:51,949
I play over on the right wing.

74
00:03:51,949 --> 00:03:54,049
Which side can I find you on?

75
00:03:54,529 --> 00:03:55,129
The left.

76
00:03:55,329 --> 00:03:56,949
Oh, yeah? That'll be fun.

77
00:03:58,409 --> 00:04:00,669
We'll be able to face off against each other.

78
00:04:01,209 --> 00:04:03,189
If they put you back in, that is.

79
00:04:03,369 --> 00:04:06,569
I've been waiting a long time for a match against Asperion.

80
00:04:06,569 --> 00:04:09,849
They are going to regret choosing you over me.

81
00:04:10,169 --> 00:04:11,909
I'm gonna crush you, Aoi.

82
00:04:14,449 --> 00:04:18,889
Oh, I guess if you're slacking so hard you aren't playing anymore, you've got nothing to worry about.

83
00:04:19,149 --> 00:04:19,809
Ha ha ha ha ha.

84
00:04:19,809 --> 00:04:21,889
Kaneda, wait!

85
00:04:22,329 --> 00:04:22,729
Nagino!

86
00:04:22,729 --> 00:04:22,869
Nagino!

87
00:04:24,869 --> 00:04:26,189
Are you okay with this?

88
00:04:26,689 --> 00:04:28,409
Playing on a team with that jerk?

89
00:04:30,109 --> 00:04:31,849
I'm sorry he said all that stuff.

90
00:04:32,149 --> 00:04:33,869
I wish I could get him to apologize.

91
00:04:34,869 --> 00:04:35,589
But...

92
00:04:35,589 --> 00:04:36,489
No need.

93
00:04:36,869 --> 00:04:38,329
He does know how to talk.

94
00:04:39,249 --> 00:04:40,469
Motivation doesn't matter.

95
00:04:40,809 --> 00:04:42,229
If you commit, then you'll win.

96
00:04:42,789 --> 00:04:43,449
He's strong.

97
00:04:43,709 --> 00:04:45,409
And his confidence is through the roof.

98
00:04:45,809 --> 00:04:47,809
I'm guessing after Asperion rejected him,

99
00:04:48,129 --> 00:04:49,969
he busted his butt to prove them wrong.

100
00:04:50,309 --> 00:04:51,509
He's a lot bigger.

101
00:04:52,789 --> 00:04:54,389
It was like touching steel.

102
00:04:54,949 --> 00:04:56,589
Yeah, we've both worked hard.

103
00:04:56,989 --> 00:04:58,829
Been training our asses off all year.

104
00:04:59,429 --> 00:05:00,369
The whole team did.

105
00:05:00,869 --> 00:05:02,529
Under manager Satake's guidance.

106
00:05:03,209 --> 00:05:03,789
I see.

107
00:05:05,249 --> 00:05:08,929
Musashino was made up of players who weren't strong enough for the J League youth teams.

108
00:05:09,329 --> 00:05:10,929
Coach knew our skills were what mattered.

109
00:05:11,329 --> 00:05:12,689
He helped us build our physiques.

110
00:05:13,469 --> 00:05:15,709
Now that we're all playing on the same level,

111
00:05:16,229 --> 00:05:17,369
no one can beat us.

112
00:05:17,889 --> 00:05:19,489
And that includes you guys.

113
00:05:20,369 --> 00:05:21,789
Well, see ya.

114
00:05:22,129 --> 00:05:23,289
Looking forward to our match.

115
00:05:23,369 --> 00:05:23,729
Nagino.

116
00:05:24,729 --> 00:05:25,729
Manager Satake.

117
00:05:26,069 --> 00:05:26,889
How is he?

118
00:05:27,649 --> 00:05:29,949
I noticed he reacted when I mentioned your name.

119
00:05:30,589 --> 00:05:32,929
He said he wished you would call him once in a while.

120
00:05:34,789 --> 00:05:36,449
Okay, I really need to go now.

121
00:05:39,389 --> 00:05:40,849
Come on, Tachibana.

122
00:05:41,389 --> 00:05:45,689
Kaneda's just a douche and probably isn't nearly as good as he likes to think he is.

123
00:05:47,089 --> 00:05:48,329
Let's get out of here.

124
00:05:48,929 --> 00:05:49,949
How about one for the road?

125
00:05:50,429 --> 00:05:51,889
Say no more, Otomo.

126
00:05:51,889 --> 00:05:57,309
Phil, I guess if you aren't playing anymore, you've got nothing to worry about.

127
00:05:57,309 --> 00:06:13,469
Our goal for the next game is to avoid a fifth loss at all costs.

128
00:06:13,469 --> 00:06:17,589
In order to net all three points, we're starting with an aggressive formation.

129
00:06:18,629 --> 00:06:20,049
We've got midfield first.

130
00:06:20,889 --> 00:06:22,329
Sugawara's going back over the right.

131
00:06:23,169 --> 00:06:24,829
That leaves Otomo on the left.

132
00:06:24,829 --> 00:06:27,389
As for who's going to lead us all to victory.

133
00:06:28,169 --> 00:06:29,309
Uh, hi.

134
00:06:29,629 --> 00:06:32,169
I'm Kenta Yoshitsune and I'll be your captain.

135
00:06:32,429 --> 00:06:33,729
Nice to see all you guys.

136
00:06:33,929 --> 00:06:34,389
And thanks.

137
00:06:34,629 --> 00:06:36,809
My injury sort of wrecked my game something hard.

138
00:06:37,189 --> 00:06:41,929
And, uh, they said playing on B team will keep my skills up while I recover, so...

139
00:06:41,929 --> 00:06:43,229
Whoa, seriously?

140
00:06:44,229 --> 00:06:45,429
Yoshitsune's are forward?

141
00:06:45,929 --> 00:06:46,749
Oh, great.

142
00:06:47,189 --> 00:06:50,089
Now that Yoshitsune's on the team, we could have had the perfect lineup.

143
00:06:50,429 --> 00:06:53,409
But then we go and put that train wreck in as our fullback instead?

144
00:06:53,489 --> 00:06:53,649
Huh?

145
00:07:00,929 --> 00:07:02,849
Hey, where's Aoi hiding?

146
00:07:03,809 --> 00:07:06,309
He couldn't focus, so he went out for a little jog.

147
00:07:06,309 --> 00:07:06,749
What?

148
00:07:07,189 --> 00:07:08,089
Who does that?

149
00:07:08,189 --> 00:07:08,809
Wow, really?

150
00:07:09,189 --> 00:07:12,749
Why on earth is he trying to wear himself out two hours before the game starts?

151
00:07:13,089 --> 00:07:14,349
Someone went jogging?

152
00:07:14,749 --> 00:07:15,669
Yeah, an idiot.

153
00:07:15,989 --> 00:07:17,529
Known as our first-year fullback.

154
00:07:18,649 --> 00:07:20,129
Don't get bent about it!

155
00:07:20,209 --> 00:07:21,349
This is Ashito's sting.

156
00:07:21,649 --> 00:07:24,929
Whenever he needs to think about stuff, he just goes out for a long run.

157
00:07:25,469 --> 00:07:27,289
Sounds like it helps him focus, then.

158
00:07:27,489 --> 00:07:27,789
Mm-hmm.

159
00:07:27,969 --> 00:07:28,349
Mm-hmm.

160
00:07:29,089 --> 00:07:31,149
Oh, well, that's fine.

161
00:07:31,269 --> 00:07:32,249
Hang on, Yoshitsune.

162
00:07:34,409 --> 00:07:36,289
Togashi, you remember what to do, right?

163
00:07:36,989 --> 00:07:38,069
What Nozomi talked about?

164
00:07:39,029 --> 00:07:39,389
Mm-mm.

165
00:07:40,809 --> 00:07:42,169
Moving on to defense.

166
00:07:43,829 --> 00:07:46,629
Togashi, just continue to follow Fukuda's instructions.

167
00:07:46,969 --> 00:07:47,429
Got it.

168
00:07:47,949 --> 00:07:51,109
No attacking allowed until I have the defense covered first, right?

169
00:07:51,609 --> 00:07:53,149
I know it's not easy for you.

170
00:07:53,749 --> 00:07:56,509
It goes against your nature, but you're doing a great job.

171
00:07:57,269 --> 00:07:58,409
Don't lose that focus.

172
00:07:58,809 --> 00:08:00,049
The same goes for this game.

173
00:08:00,649 --> 00:08:03,469
You defend first, and you attack second.

174
00:08:03,469 --> 00:08:05,409
Wasn't planning on changing anything.

175
00:08:05,409 --> 00:08:06,529
You too, Aoi.

176
00:08:11,269 --> 00:08:12,589
Defense comes first.

177
00:08:12,929 --> 00:08:13,929
Got that, fullbacks?

178
00:08:14,269 --> 00:08:15,929
So think hard before you make a move.

179
00:08:17,069 --> 00:08:19,089
At least now we've got Yoshitsune.

180
00:08:19,529 --> 00:08:22,849
Which means even if the defenders don't stretch themselves, we can still score.

181
00:08:23,169 --> 00:08:23,969
So are we cool?

182
00:08:23,969 --> 00:08:25,029
Yeah, sure.

183
00:08:25,389 --> 00:08:31,589
But what I heard Coach say was, as long as I provide a good defense, then I can attack whenever I want.

184
00:08:32,869 --> 00:08:35,609
He mentioned an aggressive formation, didn't he?

185
00:08:35,869 --> 00:08:36,209
Mm-mm.

186
00:08:36,389 --> 00:08:37,809
Pretty sure he meant this lineup.

187
00:08:37,809 --> 00:08:37,929
Tachibana?

188
00:08:39,529 --> 00:08:40,009
Jeez.

189
00:08:40,929 --> 00:08:42,069
You and Aoi, huh?

190
00:08:42,389 --> 00:08:44,689
Really think you first years can handle a game like this?

191
00:08:44,689 --> 00:08:47,309
Look at Tachibana.

192
00:08:48,309 --> 00:08:52,369
Sure, he's getting to play, but do you really think he's going to be at his best out there?

193
00:08:52,369 --> 00:08:56,429
He's been feeling down for a while now.

194
00:08:56,649 --> 00:08:58,349
But what worries me most is Aoi.

195
00:08:59,169 --> 00:09:00,669
What is Nozomi thinking?

196
00:09:00,949 --> 00:09:02,989
Why did he decide to play him this game?

197
00:09:03,749 --> 00:09:06,209
Stop what you're doing right this instant!

198
00:09:06,209 --> 00:09:08,969
What? Why are you expending your energy this way?

199
00:09:09,229 --> 00:09:11,329
You don't have very long until the match starts.

200
00:09:11,969 --> 00:09:15,489
You mentioned before that you felt useless out there at fullback.

201
00:09:16,049 --> 00:09:18,269
I'm wondering if you still feel that way?

202
00:09:18,889 --> 00:09:23,609
Because if you don't give them results in this game, who knows how long they'll bench you!

203
00:09:24,469 --> 00:09:26,769
You will never again play as a forward.

204
00:09:28,189 --> 00:09:30,409
Maybe study Kuribayashi's plays.

205
00:09:30,809 --> 00:09:31,989
Have you watched him much?

206
00:09:32,829 --> 00:09:34,409
I'm gonna crush you, Aoi!

207
00:09:34,409 --> 00:09:39,409
Oh, by the way, I got a message from Hana earlier.

208
00:09:39,889 --> 00:09:42,009
She said she's coming to watch the game today.

209
00:09:46,009 --> 00:09:53,849
The thing is, I actually feel happy.

210
00:09:55,529 --> 00:09:56,869
You were right, you know?

211
00:09:57,509 --> 00:10:00,529
I haven't been able to accept the fact that I'm playing fullback.

212
00:10:00,529 --> 00:10:05,049
And now that I'm a starter, it just felt a bit overwhelming.

213
00:10:05,049 --> 00:10:12,289
For the past month, all I did were those boring head turns.

214
00:10:12,849 --> 00:10:15,149
I got yelled at constantly in training sessions.

215
00:10:15,849 --> 00:10:18,569
I thought maybe I was feeling nervous about the new position.

216
00:10:20,329 --> 00:10:21,749
But I can see now.

217
00:10:22,529 --> 00:10:23,709
It was more than that.

218
00:10:23,709 --> 00:10:27,849
Even though I'm a fullback, it's fine.

219
00:10:28,249 --> 00:10:29,089
I'm okay.

220
00:10:29,669 --> 00:10:31,029
I don't understand.

221
00:10:31,469 --> 00:10:32,909
It's not me at all.

222
00:10:32,909 --> 00:10:36,449
I'm okay.

223
00:10:36,449 --> 00:10:36,489
Okay.

224
00:10:37,369 --> 00:10:38,469
So Hana's coming.

225
00:10:39,089 --> 00:10:39,909
That's cool.

226
00:10:40,709 --> 00:10:42,009
She has to see a good game.

227
00:10:42,269 --> 00:10:43,389
So I need to focus.

228
00:10:44,009 --> 00:10:44,909
My mind's clear now.

229
00:10:45,409 --> 00:10:45,909
Let's go!

230
00:10:50,909 --> 00:10:51,889
He's happy?

231
00:10:52,569 --> 00:10:55,489
That's what he was trying to understand before the game?

232
00:10:55,489 --> 00:11:02,189
But more importantly, why did he only realize that when he heard Hana's name?

233
00:11:03,769 --> 00:11:06,629
It's my first match playing as a fullback.

234
00:11:06,909 --> 00:11:08,909
I used to hate the idea of switching positions.

235
00:11:09,609 --> 00:11:12,229
But it feels like my heart's finally changed somehow.

236
00:11:12,889 --> 00:11:14,429
Like something's about to happen.

237
00:11:14,909 --> 00:11:16,069
Something big.

238
00:11:16,649 --> 00:11:18,369
And I'm ready for it.

239
00:11:25,489 --> 00:11:32,269
What the?

240
00:11:32,889 --> 00:11:34,049
That guy's a forward.

241
00:11:34,209 --> 00:11:35,249
Why is he playing defense?

242
00:11:36,069 --> 00:11:38,109
They need to get a new fullback.

243
00:11:38,449 --> 00:11:39,009
I know.

244
00:11:39,249 --> 00:11:41,209
He's making a mess of the entire team.

245
00:11:43,349 --> 00:11:43,709
Ah!

246
00:11:46,469 --> 00:11:50,549
Did he seriously just fall for that lame freaking fate?

247
00:11:50,549 --> 00:11:55,549
Yes!

248
00:11:56,929 --> 00:11:57,889
Nice one, Togashi!

249
00:11:58,309 --> 00:11:58,949
Hey, Aoi.

250
00:11:59,209 --> 00:12:00,949
Can you at least block the crosses?

251
00:12:01,669 --> 00:12:04,409
I'm losing count of how many you've let through at this point.

252
00:12:04,909 --> 00:12:07,109
It's your job to block opponents from your zone.

253
00:12:07,449 --> 00:12:09,229
Even if it means you have to dive in.

254
00:12:09,709 --> 00:12:12,229
Well, if it isn't my favorite reporter.

255
00:12:13,109 --> 00:12:17,109
Is this really compelling material an insignificant local match?

256
00:12:17,369 --> 00:12:17,769
Hey!

257
00:12:17,809 --> 00:12:19,089
What is up with that?

258
00:12:19,089 --> 00:12:20,189
Ashito, Aoi!

259
00:12:20,309 --> 00:12:22,309
I mean, why is he randomly playing on defense?

260
00:12:22,829 --> 00:12:23,509
He sucks!

261
00:12:24,009 --> 00:12:26,549
I came all the way out here today to watch him play forward.

262
00:12:30,709 --> 00:12:31,429
Damn it!

263
00:12:31,689 --> 00:12:33,429
I really hate defending.

264
00:12:34,089 --> 00:12:35,849
The one-on-ones are killing me.

265
00:12:37,069 --> 00:12:38,529
I have to calm down.

266
00:12:38,969 --> 00:12:39,709
Gotta take a breath.

267
00:12:40,469 --> 00:12:41,369
Breathe, damn it!

268
00:12:41,469 --> 00:12:42,629
I'm just overexcited.

269
00:12:42,709 --> 00:12:43,429
I'm not nervous.

270
00:12:45,049 --> 00:12:47,169
Can we talk about that left back?

271
00:12:47,169 --> 00:12:49,669
Dude, I'm guessing they're short on players.

272
00:12:49,989 --> 00:12:51,429
He's got to be filling in for someone.

273
00:12:51,669 --> 00:12:53,309
It's obvious he's a total noob.

274
00:12:54,809 --> 00:12:59,029
I about died when I heard the forward from the U18 Premier League was playing.

275
00:12:59,389 --> 00:13:00,649
But he's completely harmless.

276
00:13:01,229 --> 00:13:03,169
The entire team's so freaking slow.

277
00:13:03,469 --> 00:13:06,169
It's pretty clear to me why they're on a losing streak these days.

278
00:13:07,009 --> 00:13:08,989
Just don't do what you did last time.

279
00:13:08,989 --> 00:13:11,349
I'm sure you thought it was great, but don't.

280
00:13:15,349 --> 00:13:19,789
I mean, last time I saw him play, he was involved with every single goal the team made!

281
00:13:19,949 --> 00:13:21,509
I was so excited to see him in action!

282
00:13:22,189 --> 00:13:23,509
He's horrible in that position!

283
00:13:23,869 --> 00:13:26,489
Looking all over the place like a paranoid rooster, really?

284
00:13:26,869 --> 00:13:30,609
He should be looking upfield and following the center back's instructions, but no!

285
00:13:30,609 --> 00:13:32,929
You don't understand.

286
00:13:33,209 --> 00:13:35,149
A fullback is just like the Lance and Shogi!

287
00:13:35,889 --> 00:13:38,169
Like the Lance and Shogi or something.

288
00:13:39,029 --> 00:13:41,649
Why are they doing this?

289
00:13:41,649 --> 00:13:49,809
For the past month, I did more than just basic training.

290
00:13:50,269 --> 00:13:52,309
I perfected my head-turning moves.

291
00:13:52,569 --> 00:13:53,049
The wing!

292
00:13:53,729 --> 00:13:54,669
Oh, no!

293
00:13:55,029 --> 00:13:55,589
Ashito!

294
00:13:55,889 --> 00:13:57,269
The trains overwhelm you!

295
00:13:57,589 --> 00:13:58,549
Just stay calm.

296
00:13:59,629 --> 00:14:00,809
Just stay calm.

297
00:14:01,809 --> 00:14:02,749
Just stay calm.

298
00:14:02,769 --> 00:14:03,529
What are you doing?

299
00:14:03,669 --> 00:14:04,289
Tackle him!

300
00:14:04,569 --> 00:14:05,469
Calm down.

301
00:14:07,469 --> 00:14:08,829
Just calm down.

302
00:14:09,169 --> 00:14:10,709
You can do it!

303
00:14:11,649 --> 00:14:14,729
You can do it!

304
00:14:14,909 --> 00:14:15,489
Defender!

305
00:14:29,489 --> 00:14:29,969
Otomo!

306
00:14:30,449 --> 00:14:31,809
Don't let them drag you out!

307
00:14:31,969 --> 00:14:33,329
Get in front of number 26!

308
00:14:33,729 --> 00:14:34,289
Right!

309
00:14:35,469 --> 00:14:35,949
Seriously?

310
00:14:36,669 --> 00:14:37,189
What?

311
00:14:37,449 --> 00:14:38,369
Where's he going?

312
00:14:38,889 --> 00:14:41,069
If he's over there, I don't have room to attack.

313
00:14:41,069 --> 00:14:42,949
Look, that's their defensive midfielder.

314
00:14:43,129 --> 00:14:43,789
Can't go there.

315
00:14:44,109 --> 00:14:45,889
My only option is to pass it.

316
00:14:48,209 --> 00:14:49,309
What are you doing?

317
00:14:49,449 --> 00:14:50,089
Tackle him!

318
00:14:50,369 --> 00:14:51,249
He's wrong.

319
00:14:51,609 --> 00:14:53,229
I'm not going to tackle a player.

320
00:14:53,729 --> 00:14:55,069
What I need to tackle is...

321
00:14:55,589 --> 00:14:56,069
The space!

322
00:14:56,069 --> 00:14:56,649
The space!

323
00:14:56,649 --> 00:15:02,949
That was a really impressive move he made.

324
00:15:03,429 --> 00:15:05,269
He started running even before the pass.

325
00:15:05,649 --> 00:15:07,189
He read the path of it perfectly.

326
00:15:08,049 --> 00:15:10,449
It's like he could already see the game playing out.

327
00:15:10,449 --> 00:15:10,489
Huh?

328
00:15:10,489 --> 00:15:19,929
Hey, did you see that?

329
00:15:20,329 --> 00:15:22,009
That move Ashito just made.

330
00:15:22,409 --> 00:15:24,029
He's doing really well at defense.

331
00:15:24,369 --> 00:15:25,149
I saw it.

332
00:15:25,249 --> 00:15:25,529
Oh!

333
00:15:26,129 --> 00:15:28,369
Hey, aren't you the girl who showed me around last time?

334
00:15:28,369 --> 00:15:32,049
Is he looking at you?

335
00:15:39,529 --> 00:15:41,409
How rude. What was that about?

336
00:15:41,889 --> 00:15:44,749
Who sees a cute girl that's cheering for him and then ignores them?

337
00:15:45,829 --> 00:15:48,829
He's in the middle of a game. He's trying to concentrate.

338
00:15:49,429 --> 00:15:51,009
My bad. I'm being distracting.

339
00:15:53,589 --> 00:15:56,729
I was right. It worked really well.

340
00:15:56,729 --> 00:15:59,409
Keep eyes on the player with the ball first,

341
00:15:59,569 --> 00:16:01,649
then look to the players without the ball next.

342
00:16:01,929 --> 00:16:05,589
I know it's basic soccer technique, but I get it now.

343
00:16:05,709 --> 00:16:08,469
It makes more sense. It's all about dots.

344
00:16:08,749 --> 00:16:10,549
About players being the dots.

345
00:16:11,069 --> 00:16:12,569
Well, more like where they're standing.

346
00:16:12,969 --> 00:16:14,829
Then if you connect the dots with a line,

347
00:16:15,009 --> 00:16:16,709
that line is where the spaces are.

348
00:16:17,169 --> 00:16:20,429
If there aren't any good spaces, then all you have are stagnant dots.

349
00:16:20,669 --> 00:16:22,689
No point in tackling a dot that won't move.

350
00:16:22,969 --> 00:16:25,589
You gotta run to block the space they're gonna try and get to.

351
00:16:25,589 --> 00:16:27,449
That'll be way more effective.

352
00:16:28,649 --> 00:16:29,469
Dang it!

353
00:16:29,789 --> 00:16:31,209
Azito! They're countering!

354
00:16:34,509 --> 00:16:36,309
So when I'm turning my head,

355
00:16:36,509 --> 00:16:39,869
I have to note the spaces the opponent might be planning to use,

356
00:16:39,969 --> 00:16:41,369
not just their positioning.

357
00:16:42,329 --> 00:16:43,169
Over there!

358
00:16:43,389 --> 00:16:44,449
Hey! What?

359
00:16:44,449 --> 00:16:48,449
What the...

360
00:16:50,129 --> 00:16:56,309
Are you blind? That's a foul!

361
00:16:57,309 --> 00:16:57,709
Owie!

362
00:16:59,509 --> 00:17:01,669
Why would you let them draw you out like that?

363
00:17:01,789 --> 00:17:04,709
You just left a stupid amount of space open in your area!

364
00:17:06,229 --> 00:17:08,809
Players are constantly moving and changing strategies,

365
00:17:09,209 --> 00:17:11,749
so the spaces they want to use are always shifting as well.

366
00:17:11,749 --> 00:17:14,029
Was my interception earlier a coincidence?

367
00:17:14,629 --> 00:17:15,789
Just pure luck?

368
00:17:16,429 --> 00:17:16,809
Owie!

369
00:17:17,409 --> 00:17:18,049
Come here.

370
00:17:20,729 --> 00:17:21,429
Tell me.

371
00:17:21,709 --> 00:17:23,229
How did you fail this time?

372
00:17:24,589 --> 00:17:26,629
You had one successful interception.

373
00:17:26,829 --> 00:17:27,789
Why do you think that is?

374
00:17:28,169 --> 00:17:29,709
Well, I, um...

375
00:17:29,709 --> 00:17:31,189
On that particular move,

376
00:17:31,509 --> 00:17:32,829
did you look at the other players?

377
00:17:33,089 --> 00:17:34,049
Of course I did!

378
00:17:34,289 --> 00:17:35,229
That's how I planned.

379
00:17:35,429 --> 00:17:36,869
I knew where the ball was gonna go,

380
00:17:37,069 --> 00:17:38,109
and so I blocked it.

381
00:17:38,109 --> 00:17:39,309
Right.

382
00:17:39,989 --> 00:17:41,249
It was the perfect solution.

383
00:17:41,809 --> 00:17:42,249
Huh?

384
00:17:42,489 --> 00:17:45,369
So was the instruction you gave Otomo just before.

385
00:17:46,369 --> 00:17:47,389
During that play,

386
00:17:47,769 --> 00:17:49,489
you changed Otomo's direction.

387
00:17:49,969 --> 00:17:51,409
You told him to head out to the left.

388
00:17:52,069 --> 00:17:54,409
Because that blocked the route they were planning to use,

389
00:17:54,469 --> 00:17:55,409
and they couldn't link up.

390
00:17:55,889 --> 00:17:56,709
Isn't that right?

391
00:17:56,709 --> 00:17:58,329
Um, yes, sir.

392
00:17:59,229 --> 00:18:01,449
Otomo was gonna head to the middle as planned,

393
00:18:01,589 --> 00:18:04,229
but I saw that Shimizu was already there covering it.

394
00:18:04,969 --> 00:18:05,509
Then what?

395
00:18:06,229 --> 00:18:06,709
Well then...

396
00:18:07,609 --> 00:18:09,349
The opponent had to give up on the wing,

397
00:18:09,669 --> 00:18:12,129
so the only play he could make was to move centrally.

398
00:18:12,669 --> 00:18:14,609
But Tachibana was on his way from behind.

399
00:18:15,269 --> 00:18:18,249
Of course, Shimizu was already in a mega-strong position.

400
00:18:19,189 --> 00:18:21,109
After that, there were hardly any moves left

401
00:18:21,109 --> 00:18:22,469
that the opponent could even make.

402
00:18:23,029 --> 00:18:23,849
So, yeah.

403
00:18:23,849 --> 00:18:26,969
You really do have good vision.

404
00:18:27,809 --> 00:18:28,209
Oh?

405
00:18:29,009 --> 00:18:30,509
Because you see it so well,

406
00:18:30,769 --> 00:18:33,269
I want you to take it one step further, okay?

407
00:18:33,969 --> 00:18:35,669
Two times during the game now,

408
00:18:35,769 --> 00:18:36,869
you saw the space.

409
00:18:37,269 --> 00:18:39,309
It was successful one time, but not the other.

410
00:18:39,949 --> 00:18:41,429
So what did you do differently?

411
00:18:42,569 --> 00:18:43,009
Oh.

412
00:18:43,549 --> 00:18:44,589
I get it.

413
00:18:45,849 --> 00:18:47,429
We're the ones in control!

414
00:18:48,129 --> 00:18:48,749
Hurry it up!

415
00:18:48,909 --> 00:18:49,809
Let's go for the opener!

416
00:18:50,309 --> 00:18:50,829
Damn it!

417
00:18:50,829 --> 00:18:52,569
It seems like no one on our team

418
00:18:52,569 --> 00:18:53,949
is getting any time on the ball!

419
00:18:54,409 --> 00:18:54,829
Otomo!

420
00:18:55,629 --> 00:18:57,069
Go a little more central!

421
00:18:57,389 --> 00:19:00,169
Trust me, Takashima and I have this side covered!

422
00:19:01,009 --> 00:19:01,489
Shimizu!

423
00:19:01,789 --> 00:19:03,389
I'm gonna mark their number 26!

424
00:19:04,149 --> 00:19:05,029
Okay, got it.

425
00:19:05,409 --> 00:19:07,669
What made that first interception successful

426
00:19:07,669 --> 00:19:09,929
was that I used the players around me.

427
00:19:10,289 --> 00:19:11,269
The reason I failed

428
00:19:11,269 --> 00:19:12,869
was because when I spotted the space,

429
00:19:12,929 --> 00:19:14,029
I ran to it myself.

430
00:19:14,549 --> 00:19:16,949
And that created a wide opening in my zone,

431
00:19:16,949 --> 00:19:18,949
which the other guy ran into.

432
00:19:19,369 --> 00:19:20,629
Since I'm in back,

433
00:19:20,829 --> 00:19:23,149
I can see all of the players and spaces.

434
00:19:23,569 --> 00:19:25,309
I can use this to my advantage

435
00:19:25,309 --> 00:19:26,709
and block those spaces

436
00:19:26,709 --> 00:19:28,749
by shouting instructions to my teammates!

437
00:19:30,829 --> 00:19:31,769
Hey, Otomo!

438
00:19:32,189 --> 00:19:33,689
You gotta shuffle further center!

439
00:19:33,689 --> 00:19:35,549
They're about to come for that space!

440
00:19:38,349 --> 00:19:39,709
Someone, please cover!

441
00:19:39,949 --> 00:19:40,349
Anyone!

442
00:19:40,749 --> 00:19:41,149
Ugh!

443
00:19:41,149 --> 00:19:47,249
One minute you play like a noob

444
00:19:47,249 --> 00:19:48,449
and the next you're amazing.

445
00:19:48,949 --> 00:19:50,189
You're a weird first year.

446
00:19:51,849 --> 00:19:52,909
Thanks for that!

447
00:19:53,129 --> 00:19:54,249
It's quite motivating!

448
00:19:55,309 --> 00:19:57,009
Wait, what did he say?

449
00:19:57,829 --> 00:19:58,429
Anyway,

450
00:19:59,169 --> 00:20:00,749
let's go score some goals!

451
00:20:08,269 --> 00:20:10,189
Not a bad return there.

452
00:20:11,149 --> 00:20:13,789
Where do you think you're going, punk?

453
00:20:13,889 --> 00:20:15,149
Nowhere if he's blocked!

454
00:20:15,429 --> 00:20:15,869
Oh, no!

455
00:20:16,229 --> 00:20:17,729
Those two are coming for him!

456
00:20:18,709 --> 00:20:19,149
Yoshitsune!

457
00:20:19,469 --> 00:20:19,949
Pass!

458
00:20:20,289 --> 00:20:21,369
They have you covered!

459
00:20:34,609 --> 00:20:35,449
My gosh.

460
00:20:35,449 --> 00:20:41,289
I guess the B team isn't ready

461
00:20:41,289 --> 00:20:42,409
for advanced moves.

462
00:20:42,849 --> 00:20:43,929
That's too bad.

463
00:20:44,749 --> 00:20:46,729
Yoshitsune plays at a much higher level.

464
00:20:47,189 --> 00:20:48,029
When he has the ball,

465
00:20:48,249 --> 00:20:50,149
the others just need to cover the open spaces.

466
00:20:50,989 --> 00:20:52,869
See how they're all facing the same way?

467
00:20:53,069 --> 00:20:54,189
That's because the opponents

468
00:20:54,189 --> 00:20:55,409
are stuck behind them.

469
00:21:02,589 --> 00:21:03,189
Yoshitsune!

470
00:21:03,189 --> 00:21:03,829
Yoshitsune!

471
00:21:05,829 --> 00:21:06,269
Intercept!

472
00:21:06,469 --> 00:21:07,869
We can't let him hold on to it

473
00:21:07,869 --> 00:21:08,689
for too long!

474
00:21:13,549 --> 00:21:14,649
He didn't fall!

475
00:21:20,249 --> 00:21:21,169
Nice try!

476
00:21:22,869 --> 00:21:24,629
This guy's a piece of work.

477
00:21:24,829 --> 00:21:26,729
He just faked those jerks out on his own

478
00:21:26,729 --> 00:21:28,989
that created all this open space for us.

479
00:21:29,529 --> 00:21:30,329
Back at ya!

480
00:21:30,329 --> 00:21:56,029
He's the kind of player everyone can trust and rely on.

481
00:21:56,029 --> 00:21:58,169
Everything a forward should be.

482
00:21:58,829 --> 00:21:59,669
How's he do it?

483
00:22:00,309 --> 00:22:01,809
No way I could ever be like that.

484
00:22:02,229 --> 00:22:02,889
Yoshitsune!

485
00:22:03,489 --> 00:22:03,749
Huh?

486
00:22:04,389 --> 00:22:05,089
Great game.

487
00:22:05,389 --> 00:22:06,489
I want to be like you.

488
00:22:06,849 --> 00:22:08,349
And I sincerely mean that.

489
00:22:08,869 --> 00:22:09,949
Please teach me how.

490
00:22:10,309 --> 00:22:10,849
Hmm.

491
00:22:11,609 --> 00:22:12,809
Wait, don't tell me.

492
00:22:13,249 --> 00:22:14,169
You're that guy.

493
00:22:14,709 --> 00:22:15,229
Defense.

494
00:22:15,809 --> 00:22:16,569
Aoi, right?

495
00:22:17,369 --> 00:22:19,389
A lot makes sense after seeing you play.

496
00:22:20,029 --> 00:22:20,349
Huh?

497
00:22:20,349 --> 00:22:24,249
Fukuda, he speaks highly of you

498
00:22:24,249 --> 00:22:26,129
to the A-team.

499
00:22:27,309 --> 00:22:30,049
Listen, you don't have to be like me.

500
00:22:31,329 --> 00:22:33,689
You're following the path you're supposed to

501
00:22:33,689 --> 00:22:34,649
all on your own.

502
00:24:05,986 --> 00:24:27,546
Next time on Awashi, Wind of Change.

